<title>FRANCE: Plastic Omnium sees 1997 profit rise.</title>
<headline>Plastic Omnium sees 1997 profit rise.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-07-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Plastic Omnium, a French plastics company specialising in bumpers and other auto parts, said on Thursday that it expected to report significantly higher first-half profits and a full-year rise exceeding 10 percent.</p>
<p>&quot;Net earnings for the six months ended June 30, 1997, will rise significantly compared to first-half 1996 and indicate a full year increase of more than 10 percent,&quot; it said in a statement disclosing a five percent rise in its 1997 first-half sales to 3.99 billion francs.</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom, +33 1 4221 5452</p>
</text>
